<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Plymouth Colony</h1><p class="st-meta">1620 CE – 1691 CE · capital Plymouth</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The settlement founded by the Mayflower Pilgrims in 1620, remembered for the Mayflower Compact and the 1621 harvest feast with the Wampanoag.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>English Separatists who had left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-england">Church of England</a>, many of them after years of exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leiden">Leiden</a>, sailed on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayflower">Mayflower</a> in 1620 and landed at Plymouth on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-cod-bay">Cape Cod Bay</a>. Before landing, 41 men signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayflower-compact">Mayflower Compact</a>, agreeing to form a civil body politic. Half the settlers died in the first winter.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Pilgrims survived with help from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/wampanoag-confederacy">Wampanoag Confederacy</a>, whose sachem <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massasoit">Massasoit</a> made an alliance with them in 1621. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-bradford-governor">William Bradford</a>, governor for most years until 1657, wrote the history <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/of-plymouth-plantation">Of Plymouth Plantation</a>. The colony had no royal charter, governing itself through an annual General Court of freemen, and lived by farming, fishing and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a>. It remained small, with perhaps 7,000 people by 1690.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-philips-war">King Philip's War</a> in 1675 to 1676 devastated the colony. It was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dominion-of-new-england">Dominion of New England</a> in 1686, and after that collapsed, the charter of 1691 merged Plymouth into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-massachusetts-bay">Province of Massachusetts Bay</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/plymouth-colony.jpg" alt="Plymouth Colony" width="320" height="256"><figcaption>Image: Hoodinski · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plymouth_Colony_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1620 CE – 1691 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Plymouth</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>John Carver, William Bradford, Edward Winslow</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Separatist Puritanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>New Plymouth</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1656&amp;focus=plymouth-colony" aria-label="Plymouth Colony on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2962 684 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Plymouth Colony lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3282 940L4970 663M3282 940L3277 927M3282 940L3277 927"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4970 663h0M3277 927h0M3277 927h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3282 940h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3282 940h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Plymouth. <a href="/atlas?year=1656&amp;focus=plymouth-colony">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
